  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (e.g., -0.25) or when recent prices show downward momentum.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoots following sharp price spikes — especially in the first 5–7 days of the 30-day horizon.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above recent 10-day average, reduce by 5–10% in next 3–5 days.",
    "Increase downward bias in early horizon (days 1–7) if sentiment is neutral or negative, to account for lagged market reactions.",
    "Avoid over-optimistic forecasts when sentiment is flat (0.00) — use recent 18-day average as baseline anchor."
  ]
